On Sat, Apr 29, 2000 at 07:04:48PM +0900, G. Hugh Song wrote:
> Expected 1, not 2 program headers
> ... Image loaded into memory, entry @ 0x0
> MILO: Failed to load the kernel
> MILO>
> 
I think we should explicitly direct the linker to put
everything into the single segment.
Patches for 2.3.99pre6 and 2.2.15pre20 attached.

Ivan.

--XsQoSWH+UP9D9v3l
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=us-ascii
Content-Disposition: attachment; filename="lds2.2.patch"

--- 2.2.15pre20/arch/alpha/vmlinux.lds	Wed May 14 09:41:00 1997
+++ linux-2.2/arch/alpha/vmlinux.lds	Tue May  2 16:55:29 2000
@@ -1,10 +1,11 @@
 OUTPUT_FORMAT("elf64-alpha")
 ENTRY(__start)
+PHDRS { kernel PT_LOAD ; }
 SECTIONS
 {
    . = 0xfffffc0000310000;
    _text = .;
-   .text : { *(.text) }
+   .text : { *(.text) } :kernel
    .text2 : { *(.text2) }
    _etext = .;
 

--XsQoSWH+UP9D9v3l
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=us-ascii
Content-Disposition: attachment; filename="lds2.3.patch"

--- 2.3.99pre6/arch/alpha/vmlinux.lds	Fri Feb 25 09:36:04 2000
+++ linux-2.3/arch/alpha/vmlinux.lds	Tue May  2 15:13:03 2000
@@ -1,10 +1,11 @@
 OUTPUT_FORMAT("elf64-alpha")
 ENTRY(__start)
+PHDRS { kernel PT_LOAD ; }
 SECTIONS
 {
   . = 0xfffffc0000310000;
   _text = .;
-  .text : { *(.text) }
+  .text : { *(.text) } :kernel
   _etext = .;
 
   /* Exception table */

