You can mix-and-match stuff between different releases if they differ
in a minor version.  Only when switching major versions, like between
5.x and 6.y, you may run into troubles although even that is not given.
Dependencies may mean that sometimes you may need to update more than
you originally planned. :-)

> If PAM is
> the problem though, why does it work when a shell script execs init?

I do not know if PAM is really a problem.  As I noted before this
assumption does not seem to be consistent with what you write somewhere
else.  A careful documentation reading can be a good idea.

> But apparently PBS doesn't
> actually log users

If whatever that PBS is does not pay attention to a login shell
and works around PAM to provide its own login then you will have
to update it to go through libraries instead of manipulating
account information directly.

